{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j = (t, s) : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0002": "$j$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$t(s^{-1}(\\{u\\}))$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$j$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b7d5e0905dfb596c0813e525e0900a7d9720fc20c953e8ff042ad33f45bf59c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a0d261c9c3a8703de72105146a0f3b66c4100ce34f608d3734cecbd5fb44af06", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a pre-relation.\nIf <MATH_0002> is a pre-equivalence relation, then loosely speaking\nthe ``orbits'' of <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004>\nare the subsets <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006>. However, if <MATH_0007> is just a\npre-relation, then we need to take the equivalence relation generated\nby <MATH_0008>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6786495e1073be55f3abc005ffba20fb2d91e8282813afe673b011d6de0dff30", "unit_id": "tag:048M:prose-0001"}
